    "body": "I added this option because almost all tests in the module would have to be rewritten in order to create the temporary config file. I thought that option would be quite clunky as opposed to just checking for an env var. I also couldn't find an example of another program who uses a `credential_process` env var that could conflict with this.\r\nWith that being said, I'd appreciate some advice in this case. Should I stick with the env var even if it is not technically supported for the sake making the tests more readable and concise or should I rewrite all of them? Is there another way around this?\r\nThanks in advance.",
